From: Cubewood <330162352+Cubewood@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:01:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] UK junctions: Give Way lines at every minor mouth and
 roundabout entry, at the mouth; UK kerb radii

A UK level painted Give Way lines only where OSM maps a give-way node, at
MapNG's stop point (8 m or more from the junction node), so most minor
roads met the main road with no line and the mapped ones sat inside the
main road or metres back from it.

New file services/ukJunctions.js:
- impliedGiveWays: at every junction with no signals, the minor arms give
  way (road class, then the road carrying on by name or ref, then the
  straightest pair of arms); every roundabout entry gives way to the ring.
  Not where a dual carriageway starts or a one-way road merges at a
  shallow angle. A junction where OSM maps a control on an arm this rule
  gives priority is left as OSM has it.
- junctionMouth: Stop, Give Way and roundabout lines stand with their near
  edge 0.1 m off the carriageway they meet (TSM 3 2.3.1 to 2.3.4), square
  to their road, kerb to centre line or full width (one-way roads, kerb to
  centre under 2.75 m, TSM 3 2.3.2); the centre line follows uneven
  lanes:forward / lanes:backward. 1009A across the rest of a two-way mouth.
  The arm's own carriageway never counts as the road it meets. No line
  where none fits off the carriageways (a link inside a junction), in a
  dual carriageway's gap with less than 5 m behind the line, or on service
  roads, driveways and parking aisles (drawn as paving, no carriageway).
- Roundabout entries get 1003.1 (200 mm, 300 mm over 40 mph), no triangle.
- UK_CORNER_RADII: kerb returns 6 m between residential and unclassified
  streets, 4 m on living streets, 10 m with tertiary roads and up
  (Creating Places, DOE NI 2000, Table 4, para 16.27), passed to the
  sidewalk corners as options.cornerRadii; where the full radius does not
  fit, a metre less at a time down to 4 m, then MapNG's half and quarter.
  Other countries keep MapNG's table and tries.

roadMarkingCuts: crossingCarriagewaysAt lists the carriageway segments across a direction.
Signal Stop lines stay at the signal's stop point (the AI stops there),
kerb to the (lane-split) centre line.

